agentd-core — third-party material included in this crate
=========================================================

This crate's own source is AGPL-3.0-only (see the repository's LICENSE). One
set of files in it comes from elsewhere and carries its own terms. It is named
here because this notice ships inside the published package: attribution has
to travel with the copy.

The Personal Agent Protocol (https://personalagentprotocol.org), whose
repository is https://github.com/personal-agent-protocol/personal-agent-protocol.

`tests/companies/vendor/**`
   The draft agentd's Personal Agent support is built against, copied
   verbatim at commit 95fcbf22c5991a0090061aed3dbeb68c0ea575e0 (2026-10-16),
   which `tests/companies/vendor/PIN` names with the upstream path of every
   file: the 19 JSON Schemas of the draft's Company kit (`schemas/`, from
   `kit/company/schemas/`), and the Markdown renderings of the specification,
   the Operations extension and the guides (`spec.md`, `operations.md`,
   `guides.md`). The files are unmodified.
   Licence: **Apache-2.0** — the specification and its documentation,
   examples included, are published under it. The full text is at
   `tests/companies/vendor/LICENSE`, copied alongside the files as that
   licence requires.
   The licence does not cover the names "Personal Agent Protocol" and
   "Poppy", the logo, or the design of the protocol's site. The vendored files
   keep the names as upstream wrote them, which is a copy, not a use of them:
   agentd's own surface uses neutral names (`companies`, `company`), and the
   protocol's wire constants, which contain its name, live in one module
   (`src/companies/wire.rs`).

The schemas are read as data by the fake Company the tests run against
(`src/companies/mock/kit.rs` embeds them): test scaffolding compiled only into
debug builds and builds with `internal-mocks`, and only with `oauth` (and the
default `tls`). No release binary carries them. The pages are test input: the
conformance suite holds the draft sentences its checks quote to them.
